----------------------------------------------------------------------
[English Title of the Software]

   A Parallel Visual Programming Environment KLIEG


[Features of the Software]

KLIEG is a parallel visual programming environment in which a user can
develop a parallel program by editing visuals (e.g., icons
representing processes and lines representing streams) on the screen.
A program developed in the KLIEG environment will be translated into 
KL1 codes and then executed efficiently.
The execution process is animated by the KLIEG tracer.

[Required Environment]

We checked that our software can run on SparcStation 10/20s with
Solaris 2.3J, KLIC-2.002, Amulet-1.2, gcc-2.7.2, and libg++-2.7.1.
We expect that our software can run on other unix boxes possibly with
minor modifications.

