[How to Install]

1. Installation of klic and Amulet

Before installation of KLIEG, in addition of g++, the following software:

  klic 2.002	ftp://ftp.icot.or.jp/ifs/symbolic-proc/unix/klic/klic.tgz
  Amulet 1.2	http://www.cs.cmu.edu/afs/cs/project/amulet/amulet1/amulet.tar.Z

must be properly installed.
After installation of Amulet 1.2, if you use libg++ 2.7.0 or later, 
replace -liostream in AMULET_DIR/bin/Makefile.vars.gcc.Sun with -stdc++.

Notice that the current version of KLIEG cannot be compiled with Amulet 2.0.

2. Installation of KLIEG

Modify KLIEG_DIR in Makefile appropriately and then build and install
KLIEG as follows:

> make
> make install 

Notice that, with -O2 option, g++ cannot compile tracer/tracer-types.cc. 

[Getting Started]

KLIEG requires a working directly, which can be specified by the
environment variable KLIEG_WORK_DIR.  

To start a KLIEG session, just execute KLIEG_DIR/bin/klieg and 
an editor window will appear.
Pressing the middle button will open the toplevel menu (see
manual/editor.eps).
You can create a new process definition (choose "process") or
load a sample program (choose "Load") from the example directory.
